  "cross_check_warnings": [
    "rules/05-hx4s20-target.md states the board clock is 25 MHz @ R7 based on an older HX4S20 DEMO set (0_cnt1s T1S=24999999 and an Ethernet demo with create_clock -period 40). For HX4S20C this is WRONG: three independent sources in this resource pack give 50 MHz. Treat 50 MHz as authoritative and update that rules file.",
    "IOSTANDARD is genuinely ambiguous: the Ethernet DEMO (33) uses LVCMOS25 on pins that every other DEMO drives as LVCMOS33, including R7, B2, E7 and F7. The same physical pin cannot be both. Bank voltage must come from 3_原理图 before .adc generation.",
    "Pin A2 serves as KEY[0] in 6_cnt10/HX_CESHI_EG4S_BORD but as rst_n in 0_cnt1s/10_PLL_TEST/13_music/16_uart_rs232. There is no dedicated reset button; the design must pick one KEY as reset or use a power-on reset. This design uses an internal power-on reset plus KEY[0] long-press, so all four keys stay available for the application."
  ],
